new file mode 100644
index 00000000..2207a186
--- /dev/null
+++ b/_pr_body_font_overhaul.md
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+# v2 font overhaul — IBM Plex Sans (user pick), real header hierarchy, bigger + high-contrast text, the ⚠ fallback
+
+The 2026-08-22 ruling ("the current font in general is hard to read — we need a font overall, esp the headers") — **the cure, not the band-aid**: the old family is replaced wholesale; the whole HUD now renders in a real, licensed family with a real weight ladder, a tabular mono surface for the NOC dashboard, and a merged glyph fallback that finally renders the warning sign the raylib default broke on.
+
+## The rulings (all user-gated, in order)
+
+1. **2026-08-22** — "the current font in general is hard to read… esp the headers." → the family overhaul (this PR).
+2. **2026-08-22/23 (lavish A/B gallery)** — 6 families rendered on the SAME real game screens (specimen text ladder, live crisis frame, title, QoS panel, NOC overlay, win toast) through the software rasterizer; KYLE (glm-4.6v) readability grades + a mechanical ⚠-coverage probe per family. **User pick: IBM Plex Sans** ("family-native mono sibling").
+3. **2026-08-23 (lavish confirm, after the correction below)** — "can we make text bigger? and high contrast colours so it's easy to read?" → the size bump + contrast pass; re-reviewed on the real render: **"looks better"**.
+
+**Correction (disclosed in the confirm session):** in the first gallery, the IBM Plex frames were silently rendered with the fallback font — the TTF download had failed and the loader fell back quietly. The pick was re-confirmed against the REAL Plex after the fix, and the loader now **fails loudly** (B1 in round 1: the loader reports failure and app + harness + palcheck refuse to run with the raylib default — verified live: both exit 2 on a missing asset; pinned by `font_guard_reports_missing_asset`). The gallery's quiet-fallback lie is impossible now.
+
+## What ships
+
+| Surface | Before | After |
+|---|---|---|
+| Body / labels | Open Sans Regular | **IBM Plex Sans Regular** (OFL) |
+| Headers — title, toasts, panel headers, crisis banner | Open Sans Regular, same weight as body | **Plex Sans SemiBold** + a size step up |
+| NOC dashboard (D key) | Open Sans digits (proportional) | **IBM Plex Mono** — tabular numerals (advance-equality pinned by `font_mono_tabular_digits`) |
+| ⚠ (U+26A0) | no glyph anywhere (the raylib default broke on it) | **merged fallback atlas** — Noto Sans Symbols 2 (OFL) contributes the missing glyph (pinned: present-with-fallback + absent-without negative control) |
+| Sizes | 10px NOC labels · 12px floor · 14px body · 22px title · 30px toasts | 12px NOC labels · 14px floor · 15px body · 24px title · 32px toasts · every panel header +1–2px |
+| Contrast (TEXT-ONLY per Rule 6) | ink_soft 4.8:1 vs canvas | **ink_soft_text 7.2:1** — a new TEXT token; the shape token keeps its pre-fold byte, so gameplay surfaces (spawn rings, card borders, bar tracks) are pixel-unchanged by the fold; NOC panel text brightened |
+
+## Determinism (the hard rules, proven)
+
+- **T1 + replay: byte-identical.** View-layer only — `harness run` over all 48 demos: **zero non-T2 failures** (T1 hashes + the replay gate + `.log.bin`/`.t1` untouched — the golden churn is PNG-only).
+- **T2 storm: cause-documented + pixel-analyzed.** Perkins r1's own pixel analysis on the reviewed sha: 152,844 px of drift = text bands + 22,086 px disclosed ink_soft swaps — **zero pipe/packet/building/map-geometry drift**. The re-bless is deliberate (the merge-last golden storm the briefing names; this branch sits on the settled v2 head post-#88 — the final combined re-bless folds the font text pixels + the sculpted-sprite pixels together).
+- **Atlas determinism across rlsw/GPU** — the merged atlas (Plex + Noto ⚠) packs through the same `LoadFontData` + `GenImageFontAtlas` machinery as the 08-15 proven loader; assets are committed (no system-font reads).
+
+## The ⚠ pipeline (rule 6 + acceptance)
+
+- The atlas loads **ASCII 32–126 + U+26A0**; glyphs the family lacks are rasterized from Noto Sans Symbols 2 and appended to the compacted glyph array (raylib's value-keyed lookup; the merged array is `MemAlloc`'d — the `UnloadFont` lifecycle owns every byte; the fallback array block is freed after the copy).
+- `draw_text_c`/`draw_text` copy **raw UTF-8 bytes** (the old rune→byte truncation was the mojibake machine; game strings stay ASCII by lint gate 6).
+- **Pins** (`app/render/font_test.odin`): the merged atlas carries a real ⚠ glyph; Plex alone lacks it (negative control — a font swap that drops the fallback fails CI); the loader reports missing/garbage assets (the exit guards' condition); the mono digits advance equally (tabular) while body letters differ (sensitivity).
+
+## Decisions & rationale
+
+- **IBM Plex Sans over Inter/Nunito/Quicksand/Atkinson** — the user's lavish pick; the family's mono sibling makes the NOC pairing native (briefing rule 4); corrected KYLE grades 4/4/4/4.
+- **SemiBold (not Bold) for headers** — real hierarchy without chunky 15px crisis text.
+- **Noto Sans Symbols 2 as the ⚠ fallback** — OFL, symbol-range coverage; only the missing glyphs enter the atlas.
+- **The size bump + the TEXT-only contrast fold** — the user's 08-23 ruling; sizes ride the existing `hud()` scale (the ×1.25/×1.50 knob stacks on top); the fold rides a NEW text token (ink_soft_text 4.8:1 → 7.2:1 vs canvas, pinned by a contrast test) while the shape token keeps its pre-fold byte — Rule 6's "palette/layout unchanged" letter holds for gameplay surfaces; NOC row height 16px fits the 15px body.
+- **Loud loader failure (B1)** — round-1 blocker: the loader's every failure path is now reported (`font_atlas_build` + `load_fonts` return ok), and app + harness + palcheck `os.exit(2)` on failure — verified live (both binaries exit 2 with the assets missing) and pinned headless.
+- **Merge order: LAST in the wave** — the golden storm collides with every in-flight PR by design; rebased onto the settled v2 head (post-#88 blender-sculpt, `ef41b6c`) and re-blessed there. The final re-bless is the COMBINED baseline: this diff's font text pixels + #88's sculpted-sprite pixels, blessed together in one pass (48/48 green; the T2 cause = the family swap + the size/contrast fold + the sprite-sculpt pixels; T1/replay byte-identical — PNG-only churn).
+
+## Verification
+
+- `tools/ci-local.sh` — **13/13 gates green** (incl. the golden harness, PP_DEBUG overlay builds, input parity, the W1 drift negative test, the font-guard refusal exit path, and the PP_DEBUG overlay-paint smoke).
+- Harness 48/48 green on the re-blessed goldens; render suite 56/56 (incl. the 4 font pins); core 236/236.
+- Before/after captures: `docs/captures/v2-font-overhaul/` (title, crisis frame, QoS, NOC, win toast, specimens, the ⚠ proof).
+- The A/B gallery + confirm trail: `.lavish/font-gallery/` + `.lavish/font-confirm/` (review surfaces, not shipped).
